The only port that uses pctty.c and has _MSC_VER defined
is the real-mode DOS port, and DOS was not a multitasking
operating system. The original code didn't introduce a 
busy loop into a multitasking operating system, but your 
OS/2 recommendation would do so.

Removal of the "&& defined(_MSC_VER)" rather 
than adding an OS/2-specific conditional means that
you may have compile problems with that file on 
djgpp afterwards.


